    <item>
      <title>6.1. Writing functions</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/functions/6.1.-writing-functions/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/functions/6.1.-writing-functions/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;61-writing-functions&#34;&gt;6.1. Writing functions&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#61-writing-functions&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To write a function in Swift, we use the keyword &lt;code&gt;func&lt;/code&gt; followed by the function&amp;rsquo;s name, parameter list, return data type, and body (the code block). A general structure of a Swift function is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;func functionName(parameter1:DataType, parameter2:DataType, ...) -&amp;gt; ReturnDataType{&#xA;    //code block&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;simple-functions&#34;&gt;Simple functions&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-functions&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For a function, the list of parameters can be empty, meaning if our function does not require any data from us to run, we do not need to define any parameters. For example, a function to print &amp;ldquo;Hello World&amp;rdquo; could be:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>6.2. Functions with parameters</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/functions/6.2.-functions-with-parameters/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/functions/6.2.-functions-with-parameters/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;62-functions-with-parameters&#34;&gt;6.2. Functions with parameters&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#62-functions-with-parameters&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now, let&amp;rsquo;s write a function that accepts parameters and do some tasks. The following code accepts the name and age of a person as parameters and prints the details.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//function definition...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;printDetails&lt;/span&gt;(name:String, age:Int){&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;        The user&amp;#39;s name is: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;name&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;.&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;        The user&amp;#39;s age is: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;age&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;.&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;        &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;name&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt; is awesome!&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;        &amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    )&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//calling the function...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;printDetails(name: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Donald&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, age: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;25&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It prints:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;The user&amp;#39;s name is: Donald.&#xA;The user&amp;#39;s age is: 25.&#xA;Donald is awesome!&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>6.3. Functions that return a value</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/functions/6.3.-functions-that-return-a-value/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/functions/6.3.-functions-that-return-a-value/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;63-functions-that-return-a-value&#34;&gt;6.3. Functions that return a value&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#63-functions-that-return-a-value&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now, let&amp;rsquo;s think about a function that accepts an array of integers as a parameter and returns the sum of the integers.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;sumOf&lt;/span&gt;(array:[Int]) -&amp;gt; Int{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; sum = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; item &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; array{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        sum &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; item&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//returns the value...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; sum&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//calling the function with an integer array&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;print(sumOf(array: [&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;]))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It prints:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can get the returned value and store it to a constant or variable:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>6.4. More on function parameters</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/functions/6.4.-more-on-function-parameters/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/functions/6.4.-more-on-function-parameters/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;64-more-on-function-parameters&#34;&gt;6.4. More on function parameters&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#64-more-on-function-parameters&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;parameter-labels&#34;&gt;Parameter labels&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#parameter-labels&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Swift functions have the ability to have completely separate internal and external parameter names. Instead of having a single parameter name, the function below has two. The first one, &lt;code&gt;with&lt;/code&gt; is an external parameter name, which is the name that will refer to the parameter when we call the function. The second one, &lt;code&gt;vehicle&lt;/code&gt; is the internal parameter name which is the name we’ll use when we need to use the parameter within the function.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
